 "text": "Your AI agent writes code, runs commands, and reads your files. All on its own. But one poisoned README, and it leaks your keys, installs a fake package, or wipes your work. Your firewall and endpoint tools don't have the context to stop it. So we built Prismor. It sits between your agent and every tool call, and checks each one against your policy, before it runs. EcuSecrets stay placeholders. Dangerous commands get blocked. Every action is signed. EcuIt works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and twenty more. It's open source, and it runs on your machine. Ecupip install prismor. Thirty seconds. EcuStop your agents from going rogue.",
